From: mix2-port <mix2@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: mmcc-msm8998: keep the BIMC SMMU GDSC on

The bootloader leaves the display running through the MMSS SMMU with its
GDSC under hardware control. gdsc_init() switches the GDSC to software
control, which collapses it and stalls the display controller's fetches,
so the screen goes black while the framebuffer is still being scanned.

Keep the GDSC permanently on so the bootloader framebuffer keeps working
until a real panel driver takes over.
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/mmcc-msm8998.c
@@ -2623,7 +2623,7 @@ static struct gdsc bimc_smmu_gdsc = {
 		.name = "bimc_smmu",
 	},
 	.pwrsts = PWRSTS_OFF_ON,
-	.flags = VOTABLE,
+	.flags = VOTABLE | ALWAYS_ON,
 };
 
 static struct clk_regmap *mmcc_msm8998_clocks[] = {
